  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>In</mo><msub><mi>VOSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><none/><mo>'</mo><mprescripts/><none/><mo>'</mo></mmultiscripts></math> is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> oxidation state.<br />So it act as oxidising agent.<br />(ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is an amphoteric oxide.<br />(iii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>In</mo><msub><mi>RuO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi>Ru</mi><mo>'</mo></math> is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math> oxidation state. So it act as oxidising agent.<br />(iv) Red colour of ruby is due to the presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> ions in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>",
